          "content": "### End-of-unit self-check\n\n1. Which unknown in the five lesson models is governed principally by equilibrium, and which requires a deformation condition? Explain for two different examples.\n2. Identify a boundary-condition assumption in this unit that could change if a real bearing loses contact or a joint begins to slip.\n3. Form a dimensionless or unit-consistent ratio from a model response and a characteristic load or span, then explain how that ratio changes with structural stiffness.\n4. Explain how a model could satisfy overall force balance and nevertheless predict the wrong deformation field.\n5. Design a two-point numerical verification plan that does not reuse the same solver for both checks.\n6. Identify the limitation of treating code design or material yielding as if it were included in these ideal elastic analyses.\n\n**Short answer guidance:** A complete answer should use a named force path or deformation coordinate rather than generic phrases. A verification answer should specify the numerical quantity being compared and the expected reference; a validation answer should identify a relevant observation or tested physical condition."
