          "content": "### Conceptual overview\n\nAn influence line plots a response quantity at a fixed location while a unit load moves through a structure. It is not the same as a bending-moment diagram under one fixed loading arrangement. Influence lines translate moving-load problems into evaluation of response ordinates at successive axle positions. For a statically determinate simply supported bridge, reaction influence lines are linear, and a section-moment influence line is triangular. For indeterminate bridges, continuous support compatibility influences the shape. Numerical stiffness analysis can move unit loads through the mesh to obtain ordinates. Care is needed when point loads fall inside finite elements; a consistent nodal load projection should preserve virtual work, not merely allocate the full force to the nearest node."
