          "heading": "Conceptual overview",
          "content": "### Conceptual overview\n\nA linear elastic model answers a narrower question than a performance or collapse assessment. Plastic hinges can redistribute bending after local yielding, but the mechanism is highly dependent on cross-section class, lateral restraint and ductility. Stiffness degradation and connection slippage also change predicted deformation. Quantifying uncertainty adds a second layer: rather than treating a single E or load as perfectly known, one can explore response sensitivity to plausible parameter variation. Yet Monte Carlo samples drawn from invented distributions do not constitute a measured reliability model. A good computational report therefore includes assumptions, governing equations, units, verification benchmarks, reproducible inputs, mesh checks and a clear limitation statement."
